{"productId": "05c784f7-b2a1-476b-9693-4d1fbe591fde", "modelName": "Model No. 3 Schofield", "modelDescription": "Schofield Patent Revolver - In the late 1860's the U.S. Army was shopping for a breech loading fixed cartridge revolver to replace the aging 1860 Colt Army percussion revolvers. They tested the Colt single action and the S&W Model No. 3 American. The test resulted in the adoption of the Colt single action Army Model of 1873 and passing on the less powerful and more delicate 1869 S&W Model No. 3 American. Because the superior loading/reloading capability of the S&W American was recognized by Army ordnance, in 1875 Major George W. Schofield identified and Patented improvements in the design of the S&W Model No. 3 American and the Schofield Patent Revolver (Model No. 3 Schofield) was born. The S&W Model No. 3 Schofield was greatly improved over the Model No. 3 American.", "manufacturerName": "Cimarron", "subProducts": [{"isFirearm": true, "isNfa": false, "subProductId": "10e01e6d-fe3a-4828-b82e-2caf96d9f908", "description": "Cimarron, Model 3 Schofield, Revolver, 1st Model American, .45 Long Colt, 8\" Barrel, Wood Grips, Blued Finish, 6 Round Capacity\n", "imageUrls": ["https://main-images.gearfire.com/SubProductImages/14c40163-372e-4c1f-a13d-68f89d75e60f"], "isDefault": true, "manufacturerPartNumber": "CA8661", "upc": "814230101150", "attributes": [{"attributeNameId": "cd129f75-5291-4a2c-b112-feeae8b358f8", "attributeName": "Action Type", "attributeValueId": "55fa8731-23bb-4f00-a865-aae3ddf7b3d2", "valueName": "Single Action"}, {"attributeNameId": "70a78e78-6640-4f36-af23-93d050b3c0b2", "attributeName": "Capacity", "attributeValueId": "44ba4f9a-d33f-4b4c-99c2-acbca7e72010", "valueName": "6 Round"}, {"attributeNameId": "1dbab5b3-c07e-4fd5-93de-487557a9fe2d", "attributeName": "Factory Equipped Sights", "attributeValueId": "15b89746-c931-407f-af1d-ea83c38a6c08", "valueName": "Fixed Sights"}, {"attributeNameId": "5484bfc3-10d4-4ad1-ba8b-bd2973f49143", "attribut